msgid ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR Bands (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere radiances in six solar reflective channels at 500 m "
"resolution: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/cloud flagging), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrus detection), S5 "
"(1.61 µm, ice/snow/vegetation), and S6 (2.25 µm, vegetation state). Each "
"band is available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle "
"observation of land and ocean surfaces. The L1B product contains "
"geolocated, calibrated radiances produced by signal calibration, "
"re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# SLSTR VIS/SWIR-band (S1–S6)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) registrerar "
"strålning vid atmosfärens överkant i sex solreflekterande kanaler med 500 m "
"upplösning: S1 (0.555 µm, vegetation/aerosol), S2 (0.659 µm, NDVI/aerosol), "
"S3 (0.865 µm, NDVI/molnmarkering), S4 (1.375 µm, cirrusdetektion), S5 (1.61 "
"µm, is/snö/vegetation) och S6 (2.25 µm, vegetationstillstånd). Varje band "
"finns tillgängligt i nadir- och snedvy, vilket möjliggör observation av "
"land- och havsytor i två vinklar. L1B-produkten innehåller geolokaliserad, "
"kalibrerad strålning som tagits fram genom signalkalibrering, omsampling "
"till rutnät och molnmarkering.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# SLSTR Thermal Infrared Bands (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) captures "
"Top-of-Atmosphere brightness temperatures in three thermal infrared "
"channels at 1 km resolution: S7 (3.74 µm, sea/land surface temperature and "
"fire detection), S8 (10.85 µm, sea/land surface temperature and fire "
"detection), and S9 (12.0 µm, sea/land surface temperature). Each band is "
"available in nadir and oblique views, enabling dual-angle observation for "
"improved atmospheric correction and surface temperature retrieval. The L1B "
"product contains geolocated, calibrated brightness temperatures produced by "
"signal calibration, re-gridding, and cloud flagging.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."
msgstr ""
"# SLSTR termiska infraröda band (S7–S9)\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 SLSTR (Sea and Land Surface Temperature Radiometer) registrerar "
"ljustemperaturer vid atmosfärens överkant i tre termiska infraröda kanaler "
"med 1 km upplösning: S7 (3.74 µm, havs-/landytetemperatur och "
"branddetektion), S8 (10.85 µm, havs-/landytetemperatur och branddetektion) "
"och S9 (12.0 µm, havs-/landytetemperatur). Varje band finns tillgängligt i "
"nadir- och snedvy, vilket möjliggör observation i två vinklar för "
"förbättrad atmosfärskorrektion och bestämning av yttemperatur. "
"L1B-produkten innehåller geolokaliserade, kalibrerade ljustemperaturer som "
"tagits fram genom signalkalibrering, omsampling till rutnät och "
"molnmarkering.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här](https://sentiwiki.copernicus.eu/web/slstr-products#SLSTRProducts-L1"
"BProductsS3-SLSTR-Products-L1B)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal IR fire emission bands\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) has two "
"dedicated channels (F1 and F2) that aim to detect Land Surface Temperature "
"(LST). F2 Channel, with a central wavelength of 10854 nm measures in the "
"thermal infrared, or TIR. It is very useful for fire and high temperature "
"event monitoring at 1 km resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"
msgstr ""
"# Termiska IR-band för brandemission\n"
"\n"
"Sentinel-3 Sea and Land Surface Temperature Instrument (SLSTR) har två "
"dedikerade kanaler (F1 och F2) som syftar till att detektera "
"landytetemperatur (LST). Kanal F2, med en centralvåglängd på 10854 nm, "
"mäter i det termiska infraröda området (TIR). Den är mycket användbar för "
"övervakning av bränder och högtemperaturhändelser med 1 km upplösning.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här.](https://sentinel.esa.int/web/sentinel/user-guides/sentinel-3-slstr/"
"overview/geophysical-measurements/land-surface-temperature)"

msgid ""
"# Cloud base height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud base measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Molnbashöjd\n"
"\n"
"Molnbasens höjd mätt i meter (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud base pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud base in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Molnbastryck\n"
"\n"
"Tryck mätt vid molnbasen i pascal (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Effective radiometric cloud fraction\n"
"\n"
"Effective radiometric cloud fraction represents the portion of the Earth's "
"surface covered by clouds, divided by the total surface. Clouds have "
"shielding, albedo, and in-cloud absorption effects on trace gas retrieval. "
"The effective radiometric cloud fraction is an important parameter to "
"correct these effects."
msgstr ""
"# Effektiv radiometrisk molnandel\n"
"\n"
"Effektiv radiometrisk molnandel anger den del av jordytan som täcks av "
"moln, dividerad med hela ytan. Moln har skärmande effekter, albedoeffekter "
"och absorptionseffekter i molnet som påverkar bestämningen av spårgaser. "
"Den effektiva radiometriska molnandelen är en viktig parameter för att "
"korrigera dessa effekter."

msgid ""
"# Cloud optical thickness\n"
"\n"
"The cloud thickness is a key parameter to characterise optical properties "
"of clouds. It is a measure of how much sunlight passes through the cloud to "
"reach Earth's surface. The higher a cloud's optical thickness, the more "
"sunlight the cloud is scattering and reflecting. Dark blue shows where "
"there are low cloud optical thickness values and red shows larger cloud "
"optical thickness."
msgstr ""
"# Molnens optiska tjocklek\n"
"\n"
"Molntjockleken är en nyckelparameter för att karakterisera molns optiska "
"egenskaper. Den är ett mått på hur mycket solljus som passerar genom molnet "
"och når jordytan. Ju högre ett molns optiska tjocklek är, desto mer solljus "
"sprider och reflekterar molnet. Mörkblått visar var molnens optiska "
"tjocklek är låg och rött visar större optisk tjocklek."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top height\n"
"\n"
"Height of cloud top measured in meters (m)."
msgstr ""
"# Molntopphöjd\n"
"\n"
"Molntoppens höjd mätt i meter (m)."

msgid ""
"# Cloud top pressure\n"
"\n"
"Pressure measured at cloud top in Pascal (Pa)."
msgstr ""
"# Molntopptryck\n"
"\n"
"Tryck mätt vid molntoppen i pascal (Pa)."

msgid ""
"# Thermal band 10\n"
"\n"
"This thermal visualization is based on band 10 (a band is a region of the "
"electromagnetic spectrum; a satellite sensor can image Earth in different "
"bands). At the central wavelength of 10895 nm it measures in the thermal "
"infrared, or TIR. Instead of measuring the temperature of the air, like "
"weather stations do, band 10 reports on the ground itself, which is often "
"much hotter. Thermal band 10 is useful in providing surface temperatures "
"and is collected with a 100-meter resolution.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."
msgstr ""
"# Termiskt band 10\n"
"\n"
"Den här termiska visualiseringen bygger på band 10 (ett band är ett område "
"av det elektromagnetiska spektrumet; en satellitsensor kan avbilda jorden i "
"olika band). Vid centralvåglängden 10895 nm mäter det i det termiska "
"infraröda området (TIR). I stället för att mäta lufttemperaturen, som "
"väderstationer gör, redovisar band 10 själva marken, som ofta är mycket "
"varmare. Termiskt band 10 är användbart för att ge yttemperaturer och "
"samlas in med 100 meters upplösning.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här](https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-are-band-designations-landsat-"
"satellites?qt-news_science_products=0#qt-news_science_products)."

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference vegetation index is a simple, but effective index "
"for quantifying green vegetation. It is a measure of the state of "
"vegetation health based on how plants reflect light at certain wavelengths. "
"The value range of the NDVI is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDVI (values "
"approaching -1) correspond to water. Values close to zero (-0.1to 0.1) "
"generally correspond to barren areas of rock, sand, or snow. Low, positive "
"values represent shrub and grassland (approximately 0.2 to 0.4), while high "
"values indicate temperate and tropical rainforests (values approaching 1).\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserade differensvegetationsindexet är ett enkelt men effektivt "
"index för att kvantifiera grön vegetation. Det är ett mått på vegetationens "
"hälsotillstånd baserat på hur växter reflekterar ljus vid vissa våglängder. "
"Värdeintervallet för NDVI är -1 till 1. Negativa NDVI-värden (värden som "
"närmar sig -1) motsvarar vatten. Värden nära noll (-0.1 till 0.1) motsvarar "
"vanligtvis kala områden med berg, sand eller snö. Låga positiva värden "
"representerar buskmark och gräsmark (ungefär 0.2 till 0.4), medan höga "
"värden indikerar tempererade och tropiska regnskogar (värden som närmar sig "
"1).\n"
"\n"
"Mer info [här](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndvi/)."

msgid ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"The enhanced vegetation index (EVI) is an 'optimized' vegetation index as "
"it corrects for soil background signals and atmospheric influences. It is "
"very useful in areas of dense canopy cover. The range of values for EVI is "
"-1 to 1, with healthy vegetation generally around 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More infos [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) "
"and [here.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"
msgstr ""
"# Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det förbättrade vegetationsindexet (EVI) är ett ”optimerat” "
"vegetationsindex eftersom det korrigerar för markbakgrundssignaler och "
"atmosfärspåverkan. Det är mycket användbart i områden med tätt krontak. "
"Värdeintervallet för EVI är -1 till 1, där frisk vegetation vanligtvis "
"ligger kring 0.20 till 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info [här](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/evi/) och "
"[här.](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enhanced_vegetation_index)"

msgid ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI) is a vegetation index "
"that minimizes the effects of atmospheric scattering. It is most useful for "
"regions with high content of atmospheric aerosol (fog, dust, smoke, air "
"pollution). The range for an ARVI is -1 to 1 where green vegetation "
"generally falls between values of 0.20 to 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Atmospherically Resistant Vegetation Index (ARVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det atmosfärsresistenta vegetationsindexet (ARVI) är ett vegetationsindex "
"som minimerar effekterna av atmosfärisk spridning. Det är mest användbart i "
"regioner med hög halt av atmosfäriska aerosoler (dimma, damm, rök, "
"luftföroreningar). Intervallet för ARVI är -1 till 1, där grön vegetation "
"vanligtvis ligger mellan värdena 0.20 och 0.80.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info [här](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/arvi/) "
"och "
"[här.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"The Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index is similar to Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) but is used in areas where vegetative cover is low "
"(< 40%). The index is a transformation technique that minimizes soil "
"brightness influences from spectral vegetation indices involving red and "
"near-infrared (NIR) wavelengths. The index is helpful when analysing young "
"crops, arid regions with sparse vegetation and exposed soil surfaces.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"and "
"[here.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"
msgstr ""
"# Soil Adjusted Vegetation Index (SAVI)\n"
"\n"
"Det markjusterade vegetationsindexet liknar Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) men används i områden där vegetationstäcket är lågt "
"(< 40 %). Indexet är en transformationsteknik som minimerar påverkan av "
"markens ljushet i spektrala vegetationsindex som använder röda och nära "
"infraröda (NIR) våglängder. Indexet är till hjälp vid analys av unga "
"grödor, torra regioner med gles vegetation och blottad mark.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info [här](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/savi/) "
"och "
"[här.](https://eos.com/blog/6-spectral-indexes-on-top-of-ndvi-to-make-your-"
"vegetation-analysis-complete/)"

msgid ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Anthocyanins are pigments common in higher plants, causing their red, blue "
"and purple coloration. They provide valuable information about the "
"physiological status of plants, as they are considered indicators of "
"various types of plant stresses. The reflectance of anthocyanin is highest "
"around 550nm. However, the same wavelengths are reflected by chlorophyll as "
"well. To isolate the anthocyanins, the 700nm spectral band, that reflects "
"only chlorophyll and not anthocyanins, is subtracted.\n"
"\n"
"To correct for leaf density and thickness, the near infrared spectral band "
"(in the recommended wavelengths of 760-800nm), which is related to leaf "
"scattering, is added to the basic ARI index. The new index is called "
"modified ARI or mARI (also ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI values for the examined trees in [this original "
"article](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) ranged "
"in values from 0 to 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"
msgstr ""
"# Modified Anthocyanin Reflectance Index (mARI/ARI2)\n"
"\n"
"Antocyaner är pigment som är vanliga hos högre växter och ger dem röda, blå "
"och lila färger. De ger värdefull information om växters fysiologiska "
"tillstånd, eftersom de anses vara indikatorer på olika typer av växtstress. "
"Antocyanernas reflektans är högst kring 550nm. Samma våglängder reflekteras "
"dock också av klorofyll. För att isolera antocyanerna subtraheras "
"spektralbandet vid 700nm, som endast reflekteras av klorofyll och inte av "
"antocyaner.\n"
"\n"
"För att korrigera för bladens densitet och tjocklek läggs det nära "
"infraröda spektralbandet (vid de rekommenderade våglängderna 760-800nm), "
"som är relaterat till bladspridning, till det grundläggande ARI-indexet. "
"Det nya indexet kallas modifierat ARI eller mARI (även ARI2).\n"
"\n"
"mARI-värdena för de undersökta träden i [den här "
"originalartikeln](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/mari/) "
"varierade från 0 till 8.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här.](https://digitalcommons.unl.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1227&"
"context=natrespapers)"

msgid ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"The Green city script aims to raise awareness of green areas in cities "
"around the world. The script takes into account the Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) and true color wavelengths; it separates built up "
"areas from vegetated ones, making it useful for detecting urban areas. "
"Built up areas are displayed in grey and vegetation is displayed in green.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"
msgstr ""
"# Green City Script\n"
"\n"
"Green city-skriptet syftar till att öka medvetenheten om grönområden i "
"städer runt om i världen. Skriptet tar hänsyn till Normalized Difference "
"Vegetation Index (NDVI) och våglängder för äkta färger; det skiljer "
"bebyggda områden från vegetationsklädda, vilket gör det användbart för att "
"upptäcka stadsområden. Bebyggda områden visas i grått och vegetation visas "
"i grönt.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/green_city/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"The Urban Classified script aims to detect built up areas by separating "
"them from barren ground, vegetation and water. Areas with a high moisture "
"content are returned in blue; areas indicating built up areas are returned "
"in white; vegetated areas are returned in green; everything else indicates "
"barren ground and is displayed in brown colors.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/"
")"
msgstr ""
"# Urban Classified Script\n"
"\n"
"Urban Classified-skriptet syftar till att upptäcka bebyggda områden genom "
"att skilja dem från kal mark, vegetation och vatten. Områden med hög "
"fukthalt returneras i blått; områden som indikerar bebyggelse returneras i "
"vitt; vegetationsklädda områden returneras i grönt; allt annat indikerar "
"kal mark och visas i bruna färger.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_classified/)"

msgid ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"This script, made by Leo Tolari, combines true color visualization with "
"near infrared (NIR) and shortwave infrared (SWIR) wavelengths. The script "
"highlights urban areas better than true color, while still looking natural.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"
msgstr ""
"# Urban Land Infrared Color Script\n"
"\n"
"Det här skriptet, skapat av Leo Tolari, kombinerar visualisering i äkta "
"färger med våglängder i nära infrarött (NIR) och kortvågigt infrarött "
"(SWIR). Skriptet framhäver stadsområden bättre än äkta färger, samtidigt "
"som det ser naturligt ut.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/urban_land_"
"infrared/)"

msgid ""
"# NDMI for Moisture Stress\n"
"\n"
"The Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) for moisture stress can be "
"used to detect irrigation. For all the index values above 0, knowing the "
"land use and land cover, it is possible to determine whether irrigation has "
"taken place. Knowing the type of crop grown (e.g. citrus crops), it is "
"possible to identify whether irrigation is being effective or not during "
"the crucial growing summer season, as well as find out if some parts of the "
"farm are being under or over-irrigated.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"
msgstr ""
"# NDMI för fuktstress\n"
"\n"
"Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI) för fuktstress kan användas för "
"att upptäcka bevattning. För alla indexvärden över 0 går det, med kännedom "
"om markanvändning och marktäcke, att avgöra om bevattning har skett. Med "
"kännedom om vilken gröda som odlas (t.ex. citrusfrukter) går det att avgöra "
"om bevattningen är effektiv under den avgörande växtsäsongen på sommaren, "
"samt ta reda på om vissa delar av gården är under- eller överbevattnade.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi_special/#)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference moisture Index (NDMI) is used to determine "
"vegetation water content and monitor droughts. The value range of the NDMI "
"is -1 to 1. Negative values of NDMI (values approaching -1) correspond to "
"barren soil. Values around zero (-0.2 to 0.4) generally correspond to water "
"stress. High, positive values represent high canopy without water stress "
"(approximately 0.4 to 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Moisture Index (NDMI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserade differensfuktindexet (NDMI) används för att bestämma "
"vegetationens vatteninnehåll och övervaka torka. Värdeintervallet för NDMI "
"är -1 till 1. Negativa NDMI-värden (värden som närmar sig -1) motsvarar kal "
"jord. Värden kring noll (-0.2 till 0.4) motsvarar vanligtvis vattenstress. "
"Höga positiva värden representerar tätt krontak utan vattenstress (ungefär "
"0.4 till 1).\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info [här.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndmi/)"

msgid ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"The normalized difference water index is most appropriate for water body "
"mapping. Values of water bodies are larger than 0.5. Vegetation has smaller "
"values. Built-up features have positive values between zero and 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info [here.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"
msgstr ""
"# Normalized Difference Water Index (NDWI)\n"
"\n"
"Det normaliserade differensvattenindexet lämpar sig bäst för kartläggning "
"av vattenförekomster. Värdena för vattenförekomster är större än 0.5. "
"Vegetation har lägre värden. Bebyggda objekt har positiva värden mellan "
"noll och 0.2.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info [här.](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/ndwi/)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
"and exposed ground are grey or tan, and water appears blue or black.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"More info "
"[here](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) and [here.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"
msgstr ""
"# Falsk färgkomposit\n"
"\n"
"En falsk färgkomposit använder minst en osynlig våglängd för att avbilda "
"jorden. Den falska färgkompositen med nära infraröda, röda och gröna band "
"är mycket populär (ett band är ett område av det elektromagnetiska "
"spektrumet; en satellitsensor kan avbilda jorden i olika band). Den falska "
"färgkompositen används oftast för att bedöma växtlighetens täthet och "
"hälsa, eftersom växter reflekterar nära infrarött och grönt ljus medan de "
"absorberar rött. Städer och blottad mark är grå eller ljusbruna, och vatten "
"framträder som blått eller svart.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Mer info "
"[här](https://custom-scripts.sentinel-hub.com/sentinel-2/false_color_"
"infrared/) och [här.](https://eo.belspo.be/en/colour-composites)"

msgid ""
"# False color composite\n"
"\n"
"A false color composite uses at least one non-visible wavelength to image "
"Earth. The false color composite using near infrared, red and green bands "
"is very popular (a band is a region of the electromagnetic spectrum; a "
"satellite sensor can image Earth in different bands). The false colour "
"composite is most commonly used to assess plant density and health, since "
"plants reflect near infrared and green light, while they absorb red. Cities "
